<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-ASTRA H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT RISES 4 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-ASTRA H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT RISES 4 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs group Astra AB on Friday posted these earnings for the first six months of 1997, ending on June 30.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   7,014  vs  6,756</p>
<p> Sales				     21,471  vs 19,077</p>
<p> Earnings per share (Skr)		3.07  vs   2.94</p>
<p> Operating costs			 14,722  vs 12,780</p>
<p> Operating profit			 6,749  vs  6,297</p>
<p> Net financial items			260  vs    464</p>
<p> Minorities			CREDIT     5  vs	5  CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					  1,975  vs  1,933</p>
<p> Net profit				 5,039  vs  4,823</p>
<p>NOTE -- Market expectations were for a six percent rise in pre-tax profit to 7.18 billion crowns, a Reuters poll of 15 analysts found.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
